x86_64-linux  clang emits `_Unwind_Resume` and `DW.ref.__gxx_personality_v0` and cxx1 emits neither. It is about the cleanup a converting return needs, not about mangling: cxx1 builds the converted temporary straight into the return slot and hands its bytes to the caller, so nothing of this function's is left to destroy and there is no landing pad to resume from, where clang at -O0 constructs and then copies and so has an object to clean up if the copy throws. Both are permitted - the elision is the one C++11 allows here - and x86_64-windows agrees on all seven names.
arm64-darwin  the same difference, and `__Unwind_Resume` alone because Mach-O needs no personality reference symbol. See the x86_64-linux line above.
